    "scenesThatPass": [
      "MICHELLE: How much do you pay them? So demeaning.\nIRENE: I have nothing to be ashamed of. This is my life. My sex life... You’re just a little bitch.\nMICHELLE: All I’m saying is you’re on a fixed income. You should be more economical. Do you really need a young stud at your age?\nIRENE: Did you eat? I made spaghetti.",
      "REBECCA: Michelle, glad I caught you. I’m putting these on everybody’s door. It's about the neighborhood coucil's new trash-separation policy.\nMICHELLE: Oh, thank you.\nREBECCA: They're levying a pretty steep fine now if recycleables aren't properly sorted and we're having a block meeting Wednesday to organize our op…\nMICHELLE: But you're on the council, aren't you?",
      "MICHELLE: It's an interesting position anyway.\nREBECCA: That's how I like to look at it.",
      "MICHELLE: I was trying to... I was going to try to find a way to segue into this organically but there really is no graceful way so I’m just going to …\nANNA: Oh my god.",
      "ANNA: Oh my God.\nMICHELLE: I really haven’t known what to say... What is there to say? I feel stupid now for bringing it up."
    ]
  },
